.TH DXDFIR 1 "2026-09-11" "dxdfir 0.6.0" "DX_DFIR Manual"
.SH NAME
dxdfir \- DX_DFIR forensic processing pipeline front-end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dxdfir
.RI [ --version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B dxdfir process
.I SOURCE
.RB [ --pipeline
.IR elastic | sofelk ]
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --repo-root
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --extra-var
.IR KEY=VALUE ]...
.br
.B dxdfir build-car
.RI [ PROCESSED_DIR ]
.RB [ --in
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ --rebuild ]
.br
.B dxdfir verify-car
.RB [ --car-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B dxdfir car-timeline
.I CAR_DIR
.RB [ --out
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B dxdfir validate
.br
.B dxdfir verify-images
.br
.B dxdfir build-docker
.RB [ --image
.IR NAME ]...
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --repo-root
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --extra-var
.IR KEY=VALUE ]...
.br
.B dxdfir list
.br
.B dxdfir stix
.I SUBCOMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dxdfir
is the user-facing front-end of the DX_DFIR pipeline \(em an offline,
container-based digital-forensics workflow that turns raw evidence (packet
captures, disk images, memory, Windows event logs) into normalised JSON,
materialised MITRE CAR and detection events for the Elastic-native analysis
backend.
.PP
It is the top of a three-layer design: this command holds the verbs, the
.B get_sybers.dxdfir
Ansible collection holds the orchestration (one role per source, one action per
task), and the
.B get_sybers_dxdfir
Python package holds the heavy per-item processing the roles invoke.
.PP
.B dxdfir process
drives a source's role with
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
\(em preflight, then process, then verify \(em and the role's single action calls
.RB \(lq python \-m get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \(rq
for the tight loop.
.BR build-car ", " verify-car " and " car-timeline
drive the CAR lane the same way (the
.B dxdfir_car
role over the external Byakugan engine \(em see
.B BYAKUGAN_ROOT
under
.B ENVIRONMENT
\(em and the
.B get_sybers_dxdfir.carcheck
gate), while
.B validate
fronts the repository's check harness
.RB ( tests/run-checks.sh ).
The analysis backend itself (the Elastic stack under
.IR docker/elastic )
is brought up with docker compose; see its README.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "process " SOURCE
Process one evidence source. \fISOURCE\fR is one of
.BR zeek ", " evtx ", " volatility ", " plaso ", " zimmerman ", " signatures .
Idempotent: inputs that already have output are skipped (use
.B --force
to reprocess).
.TP
.BI "build-car " [PROCESSED_DIR]
Build the per-source CAR stores (car.db + superset.db + one
.IR car_<object>.jsonl
per object) from the processed tree \(em every source under it by default, or
one file/dir with
.BR --in .
A source whose store already exists is left alone unless
.B --rebuild
is given.
.TP
.B verify-car
The CAR correctness gate over the materialised CAR
.RI ( data_store/processed/car
by default, or
.BR --car-dir ):
each exercised object populated, values sane (IPs, ports, SIDs,
.I car_action
in the engine model's vocabulary), every row traceable to one artefact, the
relationship edges naming real endpoints. Run the pipeline first
(process, then build-car).
.TP
.BI "car-timeline " CAR_DIR
Build one property-rich, time-ordered CAR timeline JSONL from a source's
car.db + superset.db (or aggregate a whole tree).
.TP
.B validate
Run the repository check harness (fronts
.IR tests/run-checks.sh ).
.TP
.B verify-images
Audit the hardened
.I dxdfir/*
tool-image inventory: every expected image present and hardened, nothing
unexpected in the namespace.
.TP
.B build-docker
Build (and hardening-verify) the
.I dxdfir/*
tool images from the in-repo Dockerfiles. Fronts
.I playbooks/dxdfir-build-images.yml
(the
.B dxdfir_images
role): each image is built from its ansible-hardened Dockerfile under
.IR docker/ ,
then the hardening contract is asserted on the result (fixed non-root
.BR USER ,
.B com.get-sybers.hardened
label, no
.BR apt-get / dpkg / sudo / pip /ansible;
shell + python absent from the tool-only images). Restrict the set with
.B --image
(repeatable); rebuild existing images with
.BR --force .
Run once per host before first processing, and again after changing anything
under
.IR docker/ .
.TP
.B list
Inventory the evidence staged under
.IR data_store/raw :
for each source that
.B process
reads, the input directory and how many evidence files are present.
.TP
.BI "stix " SUBCOMMAND
The STIX 2.1 / OpenCTI exchange verbs (detections to sightings, indicators in,
sightings back); see
.BR "dxdfir stix -h" .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit. Accepted at every level, e.g.\&
.BR "dxdfir -h" " or " "dxdfir " \fICOMMAND\fR " -h" .
Each level shows its own options.
.SS process
.TP
.BR --pipeline ", " -p " " \fIelastic\fR|\fIsofelk\fR
Backend to target; selects the output destination. Default:
.BR elastic
(the processed tree the CAR lane builds from);
.B sofelk
writes the retiring SOF-ELK delivery tree instead.
.TP
.B --force
Reprocess inputs that already have output.
.TP
.BI --repo-root " PATH"
DX_DFIR repository root. Auto-detected otherwise (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.BR --extra-var ", " -e " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Pass an extra Ansible variable through to the role; repeatable. Use it to override
a role default, e.g.
.RB \(lq -e\  dxdfir_zeek_pcap_dir=/evidence/pcaps \(rq
or
.RB \(lq -e\  \(aq{\(dqdxdfir_signatures_lanes\(dq:[\(dqyara\(dq]}\(aq \(rq.
.SS build-car
.TP
.BI --in " PATH"
Single-source mode: one processed file or directory, one car.db.
.TP
.BI --out " DIR"
Output directory (single-source: this source's car dir; batch: the car/ root).
.TP
.BI --host " HOST"
Single-source mode: fallback source_host where the map derives none.
.TP
.B --rebuild
Rebuild CAR stores that already exist (after a map/coverage change).
.SS verify-car
.TP
.BI --car-dir " DIR"
The materialised CAR tree to check. Default:
.IR <repo>/data_store/processed/car .
.SS build-docker
.TP
.BR --image ", " -i " " \fINAME\fR
Build only this image (e.g.\&
.BR yara ,
.BR zeek ,
.BR volatility );
repeatable. Default: every dxdfir/* tool image.
.TP
.B --force
Rebuild even when the image already exists (docker layer cache still applies).
.TP
.BI --repo-root " PATH"
DX_DFIR repository root. Auto-detected otherwise (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.BR --extra-var ", " -e " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Pass an extra Ansible variable through to the
.B dxdfir_images
role; repeatable (e.g.\&
.RB \(lq -e\  dxdfir_runtime_uid=3000 \(rq).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DFIR_REPO_ROOT
Repository root, used when
.B --repo-root
is not given. If neither is set, the repo is found by walking up from the current
directory, then from the dxdfir binary's own location.
.TP
.B BYAKUGAN_ROOT
Root of the external Byakugan engine checkout the CAR lane drives
.RB ( build-car / car-timeline ).
Default: a
.I byakugan/
directory beside the repository. The commit the pipeline is tested against is
pinned in
.I byakugan.ref
at the repository root;
.I scripts/setup-environment.sh
provisions the checkout (recursively \(em the engine's nested submodules are
required).
.TP
.B ANSIBLE_ROLES_PATH
Set by every verb that drives
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
to the collection's roles directory so the roles resolve without installing the
collection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dxdfir
exits
.B 0
on success and propagates the exit status of the underlying
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
run or tool on failure;
.B 1
for a usage error (an unknown verb, flag or argument count);
.B 2
for a lookup error (e.g. the repo or a playbook could not be found, or no
materialised CAR to verify) and
.B 127
if a required tool is not on
.BR PATH .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Build every hardened tool image (first-run setup, or after touching docker/):
.B dxdfir build-docker
.TP
Rebuild just the YARA image:
.B dxdfir build-docker --image yara --force
.TP
Process packet captures for the Elastic-native path:
.B dxdfir process zeek --pipeline elastic
.TP
Reprocess memory images, overriding the input directory:
.B dxdfir process volatility --force -e dxdfir_volatility_memory_dir=/evidence/mem
.TP
Run only the YARA signature lane:
.B dxdfir process signatures -e \(aq{\(dqdxdfir_signatures_lanes\(dq:[\(dqyara\(dq]}\(aq
.TP
Normalise everything processed into CAR, then gate it:
.B dxdfir build-car && dxdfir verify-car
.TP
One timeline across every source:
.B dxdfir car-timeline data_store/processed/car --out /tmp/timeline.jsonl
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ansible/collections/get_sybers.dxdfir/
The Ansible collection driven by
.BR "dxdfir process" .
.TP
.I python/get_sybers_dxdfir/
The processing package (also runnable as
.RB \(lq python\ -m\ get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \(rq).
.TP
.I data_store/
Raw evidence and processed output (gitignored); the materialised CAR lands under
.IR data_store/processed/car/ .
.TP
.I docker/elastic/
The Elastic-native analysis backend (docker compose).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ansible-playbook (1),
.BR docker (1).
The processors run standalone as
.RB \(lq python\ -m\ get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \ --help\(rq.
